	(text "J4 HCTL HC-RJ45-059-4-4: 4 ports, shielded, no magnetics, no LEDs.\nEvery port: 1 = CAN_H (white-orange), 2 = CAN_L (orange): one twisted pair;\n3 = GND (white-green); 4-8 open. T568B colours, CiA 303-1 pinout,\nsame as the MES4-Flasher RJ45. Shield tabs to GND.\nFootprint: pad positions from the JLC library part, drills from the\nHCTL drawing (32 × Ø1.0, shield Ø1.7, pegs Ø3.2). Port fronts 17 mm\nin front of the pin-1 row: place them at the board edge.\nD7 H24VNT2B: ESD at the RJ45 bank."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.74 88.9 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "f8b4ce97-a657-5bf8-9009-99c68de0cbd1")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 15.24 123.19)
		(end 403.86 157.48)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "952bbcc5-a7fc-58a6-8947-f53c0307d64c")
	)
	(text "CAN bus rules (CIF §5, rules 8-9)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 125.73 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "c66aebe1-1b37-59c2-b4c2-374f5b6b1364")
	)
	(text "All five ports (DB9 + 4 × RJ45) are the same bus, wired in parallel to the module's CANH / CANL (fingers 1 / 3).\nKeep the bus a line: IPC → DB9 → this board → one RJ45 → next node → ... A port used as a branch is a stub:\nkeep each stub ≤ 0.3 m at 500 kbit/s. More long branches need a hub with its own transceivers, not more ports.\nExactly two 120 Ω terminators, at the two physical ends of the bus: bridge JP1 on the module only if this board is an end.\nAll nodes on one solid ground: pin 3 (RJ45) / pin 1 (DB9) carry it. Check with power off: CAN_H-CAN_L ≈ 60 Ω.\nNever carry 24 V in a CAN cable or connector (CIF rule 9): these jacks carry only CAN_H, CAN_L and GND.\nNo series resistors on CAN_H / CAN_L (CIF rule 8): the module must drive the 60 Ω bus directly."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 130.81 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "dcd349fc-b56e-5747-bac5-4f7f718163cc")
	)
